Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 07:59:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 037/154] feat: let the Atrium window exist without a dylib
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three gates decided that Atrium ran at all, and every one asked the Swift
dylib:

  browser_window_factory.cc   created AtriumBrowserWindow only when connected()
  atrium_feature_check.cc     IsAtriumBrowserWindowEnabled returned connected()
  atrium_main_extra_parts.cc  an early return skipped the chrome layer, the
                              collection observer and every controller-creating
                              path

After the cut connected() is always false, so the browser started as plain
Chromium. Measured by A/B on one build: 18 AtriumBrowserWindow log lines with a
dylib present, 0 without.

Removing the early return then died on
DCHECK(UIBridge::Get()->connected()) in the controller - the cascade the task
warned about, found one launch at a time. Five such DCHECKs are gone; they
asserted a precondition the cut removed.

Result, with no dylib anywhere and none loaded:

  scenario rust-core-sidebar: 2 passed, 0 failed
  4 Rust-backed sidebar pushes
  0 "UI dylib connected"

So the browser now runs its own chrome and draws its sidebar from Rust with no
Swift involved. The remaining ~149 UIBridge call sites are still to sweep.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_window_factory.cc | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_window_factory.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_window_factory.cc
index b92bf6cc20348..3f4a712d0319d 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_window_factory.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_window_factory.cc
@@ -40,7 +40,13 @@ BrowserWindow::CreateBrowserWindow(Browser* browser,
                                    bool user_gesture,
                                    bool in_tab_dragging) {
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
-  if (atrium::UIBridge::Get()->connected() && browser->is_type_normal()) {
+  // The Atrium window no longer waits for a dylib to connect.
+  // This used to read `UIBridge::Get()->connected() && ...`, which meant that
+  // after the Swift cut no Atrium window was created at all - measured by A/B
+  // on 2026-08-09, 18 window log lines with a dylib present and 0 without.
+  // Every surface, scenario and Rust-path check downstream needs a window to
+  // exist first.
+  if (browser->is_type_normal()) {
     // Little Atrium: BrowserController::CreateLittleWindow
     // brackets its own Browser::Create() call with this marker (Browser has
     // no SupportsUserData/UnownedUserDataHost slot cheap enough to stamp
